) has no proving command; the Verification section names only pytest, make lint, and make typecheck, none of which assert on the comment text in .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f10b623ced6848d8e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria / Verification section","norm_id":"nf14a4350d98e59b0","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer marks the plan done with the header comment still stale because no gate catches it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to Verification a concrete assertion, e.g. `grep -qE 're-sample|converg' .github/workflows/mirror-guard.yml` anchored on the new wording, or reference the specific line the comment must no longer contain.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the re-fetch mechanism for the live GitHub main tip (e.g. reuse the same sampling call the replication check uses) rather than leaving the source of the tip to the executor.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'merged_reachability_check re-fetches the GitHub main tip rather than comparing against the checkout-time HEAD'","Root cause describes destination_ref defaulting to 'HEAD' but does not state how the live tip is re-obtained"],"finding":"The mechanism for obtaining the 'live' GitHub main tip is unspecified (git fetch of remote main vs a GitHub API call vs re-reading a ref), leaving the executor to choose an approach for AC1.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2639abe74742789f","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause defect #2 / AC1","norm_id":"nede973760a1510f3","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor picks a fetch mechanism that differs from how the replication check samples main, producing an inconsistent comparison"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that merged_reachability_check obtains the main tip via the same mechanism _replication_check_with_lag_tolerance already uses to sample GitHub main, so both checks share one source of truth.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify that re-fetching the GitHub main tip means performing a `git fetch` of GitHub main into the local repo and targeting the freshly-fetched ref (e.g. FETCH_HEAD) in the ancestor test — not merely re-reading fetch_github_main_sha's REST SHA, which leaves the new commit object absent locally.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:289 `if _git(\"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", \"FETCH_HEAD\", destination_ref).returncode != 0:` — ancestry is checked against a local ref","src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:188-194 `fetch_github_main_sha` returns `json.loads(body)[\"sha\"]` — a SHA string only, no git object fetched","search for 'github.com' shows only REST endpoints; no `git fetch` of GitHub objects exists as a seam"],"finding":"AC-1 ('re-fetches the GitHub main tip') under-specifies the git-object plumbing: the ancestor test (`git merge-base --is-ancestor FETCH_HEAD destination_ref`) operates on LOCAL git refs, but the only GitHub-main seam (fetch_github_main_sha) returns a SHA via the REST API, not a fetched commit object. Re-reading the SHA does not place the newly-advanced GitHub main commit in the local repo, so re-sampling will re-test against the same stale local HEAD and keep failing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f504abc00f9907835","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, line 'merged_reachability_check re-fetches the GitHub main tip'; src/rebar/mirror_guard.py:289","norm_id":"n0d83a602bf2a7bd2","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A revision submitted after checkout: GitHub main advances but its new commit object is absent locally, so a re-sample against a re-read SHA still reports 'not ancestor' and the run reds — the plan's core fix does not converge."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC/step requiring the check to `git fetch` the GitHub main branch (via a new seam) each sample and use that fetched ref as `destination_ref`, so `merge-base --is-ancestor` sees the advanced tip; assert the reproduction test monkeypatches this fetch to advance the tip between sample 1 and sample 2.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add a one-line positive rationale stating why re-sampling with the replication check's shared lag knobs is the correct fit (verifies the same per-revision invariant while absorbing the same transient lag the replication half already tolerates).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan describes the defect and the shared-knobs fix but never states a 'why this approach fits' sentence (e.g. why absorbing lag by re-sampling is preferable to widening the workflow window or dropping the check)."],"finding":"The plan does not state a positive rationale for why re-sampling the reachability check (mirroring _replication_check_with_lag_tolerance) is the right fit, beyond implying parity with the sibling check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb47e7c2d06a94fec","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause / Acceptance criteria sections","norm_id":"n9f927df0479d874a","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer weighing whether to instead loosen the workflow schedule or remove the reachability check lacks the plan's stated reasoning for the re-sample choice."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"ec35273b276885d4","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f822e42f0dddbbde",3819],"description_boxes":["e91772ccb5e6ce5f",0],"file_impact":["a87c141ef4530515",3],"ticket_id":["15b98331b635c232",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":213532,"cache_write_tokens":100805,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":5034